  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed with する: {参拝|さんぱい}する (to visit a shrine/temple to pray). Applicable to both Shinto shrines ({神社|じんじゃ}) and Buddhist temples ({寺|てら}/{寺院|じいん}).\n\nAt a Shinto shrine, the standard procedure involves bowing, clapping, praying, and bowing again ({二拝二拍手一拝|にはいにはくしゅいちはい}).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {参拝|さんぱい}する: to visit and pray\n- {参拝|さんぱい}{客|きゃく}: worshippers, visitors\n- {参拝|さんぱい}{者|しゃ}: worshippers\n- {初|はつ}{参拝|さんぱい}: first visit of the year",
